WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.251
Former New Jersey Governor

00:00:01.251 --> 00:00:03.003
Chris Christie, who's challenging

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.796
Donald Trump for the 2024

00:00:04.796 --> 00:00:06.840
Republican presidential nomination

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.799
and is one of the former

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:09.968
president's most vocal critics

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.845
says he was actually questioned

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:13.805
in one of the Trump investigations,

00:00:13.805 --> 00:00:16.057
although he will not reveal which one.

00:00:16.307 --> 00:00:16.725
He did

00:00:16.725 --> 00:00:18.727
tell Kara Swisher on her podcast

00:00:18.727 --> 00:00:20.603
that he was honest in his answers.

00:00:20.603 --> 00:00:22.814
He also says he believes Trump fears

00:00:23.064 --> 00:00:24.232
that he could go to jail.

00:00:24.232 --> 00:00:25.567
Listen to this.

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:29.237
I think there's no doubt in my mind

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.406
that more nights than not

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:32.949
where he's in Bedminster or at Mar

00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:33.867
a Lago,

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:34.451
he lays down

00:00:34.451 --> 00:00:36.077
a bed, the lights go out,

00:00:36.077 --> 00:00:38.496
and he stared at the ceiling thinking

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:40.999
I could go to jail, I could go to jail,

00:00:42.584 --> 00:00:42.792
All right.

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:43.501
Let's get some more on

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:44.711
what Chris Christie had to say.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:45.211
Joining us

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.629
now is Kara Swisher,

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:47.922
the host of the podcast

00:00:47.922 --> 00:00:49.215
On with Kara Swisher.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.051
Kara, thanks very much for joining us.

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.343
He revealed to you

00:00:52.343 --> 00:00:53.261
that he's been interviewed

00:00:53.261 --> 00:00:54.345
in one of these Trump

00:00:54.345 --> 00:00:55.764
related investigations.

00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:56.890
What else did he tell you?

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.099
Well, he talked about a lot of things,

00:00:58.099 --> 00:00:59.142
but I think it's

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:01.269
probably the January 6th investigation

00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:01.978
is my guess

00:01:01.978 --> 00:01:02.937
of what he was talking about,

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:03.772
because he was referring

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:05.774
to his state of mind and his intent

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:06.900
during the insurrection,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.902
I think, or about the election fraud.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.112
But he said a lot of stuff.

00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:13.073
He was talking about his state of mind.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:15.909
He talked a lot about obviously the break

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.744
for lots of reasons.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:20.830
And I think he feels as if he has a lane

00:01:21.122 --> 00:01:21.623
to be in,

00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:23.083
even though he's way down in the polls.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.542
Everybody's way down in the polls.

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:26.586
But there's a lane if Donald Trump

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.340
has more legal problems

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:32.342
and can't continue the race, that's that

00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:33.134
that's his bad,

00:01:33.134 --> 00:01:33.802
I guess, where

00:01:33.802 --> 00:01:35.095
he thinks he can still win

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:36.554
the Republican nomination.

00:01:36.554 --> 00:01:37.305
Is that what he told you?

00:01:37.305 --> 00:01:38.431
Well, he said he's going to

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:39.140
give me an interview.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:39.766
So I don't know.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:40.308
But I you know,

00:01:40.308 --> 00:01:41.768
I maybe I'll be president.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:42.685
I'll give him an interview.

00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:44.229
But but he

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:46.397
I think he thinks there is is a lane here

00:01:46.397 --> 00:01:47.774
for someone else.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:48.817
Who's not Donald Trump,

00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:49.359
you know,

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:50.652
their political opponents,

00:01:50.652 --> 00:01:51.945
Christie and Trump.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:54.280
But Christie knows Trump really well.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.657
Yeah. Very close.

00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:55.990
What else

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:57.158
he said about some insight

00:01:57.158 --> 00:01:59.202
he had into Trump's thinking right now?

00:01:59.202 --> 00:01:59.619
Well,

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.329
I think he thinks he's scared of

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:01.955
going to jail.

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.164
And I think he's probably right.

00:02:03.164 --> 00:02:03.540
He's talking

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:04.707
he recounted a dinner

00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:06.376
that he had with him

00:02:06.376 --> 00:02:07.293
where the Christie had

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:08.169
with Trump, with Trump.

00:02:08.169 --> 00:02:09.546
And he and he talked about

00:02:09.546 --> 00:02:10.547
someone who was going to jail.

00:02:10.547 --> 00:02:11.047
Powerful.

00:02:11.047 --> 00:02:12.549
This is years and years ago,

00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:14.759
I think it was in a New Jersey senator

00:02:14.759 --> 00:02:16.427
of some sort of state senator

00:02:16.427 --> 00:02:17.595
and Trump

00:02:17.595 --> 00:02:18.888
kept saying he's really going to jail.

00:02:18.888 --> 00:02:19.889
He's really going to jail

00:02:19.889 --> 00:02:22.142
and seemed terrified with what

00:02:22.725 --> 00:02:24.185
Christie seemed to indicate.

00:02:24.185 --> 00:02:25.270
And that was interesting.

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:25.770
But that he

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.939
that he cannot imagine

00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:31.192
finally having to to to pay

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:33.278
legal the legal price that looks like

00:02:33.278 --> 00:02:34.571
he may have to buy this.

00:02:34.571 --> 00:02:35.321
Christie believe

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.198
that Trump could wind up going to jail.

00:02:37.198 --> 00:02:38.283
I think he does. I'm not.

00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:39.659
So I push back on that

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:40.285
because I felt like

00:02:40.285 --> 00:02:41.619
they're probably putting a president in

00:02:41.619 --> 00:02:42.370
jail is probably

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.414
there's some deal to be made or simply

00:02:44.414 --> 00:02:45.373
but he definitely thought

00:02:45.373 --> 00:02:46.040
the possibility

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:46.416
was there

00:02:46.416 --> 00:02:48.960
because of the possibility of jail time

00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:50.378
hanging over his head.

00:02:50.378 --> 00:02:50.962
But until then

00:02:50.962 --> 00:02:51.921
he would take advantage of it

00:02:51.921 --> 00:02:52.881
and raise money

00:02:52.881 --> 00:02:53.756
which he's already done

00:02:53.756 --> 00:02:54.966
which you did the next day.

00:02:54.966 --> 00:02:56.217
Christie obviously is running

00:02:56.217 --> 00:02:57.468
as a Republican right now.

00:02:57.468 --> 00:02:58.469
He is a Republican,

00:02:58.469 --> 00:02:59.470
but he seems to be taking

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:00.889
a very different tone

00:03:00.889 --> 00:03:02.849
on this investigation. Listen to this.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:05.560
I don't really think there's

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:06.936
anything political

00:03:06.936 --> 00:03:08.688
about what Jack Smith is doing.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:09.606
How effective is that?

00:03:09.606 --> 00:03:10.481
Calling it a witch hunt

00:03:10.481 --> 00:03:11.274
and stuff like that?

00:03:11.274 --> 00:03:12.066
It seems to be effective

00:03:12.066 --> 00:03:13.151
among his supporters.

00:03:13.151 --> 00:03:13.776
I think it's effective

00:03:13.776 --> 00:03:14.527
among his supporters.

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.237
I think once you get to a courtroom, it's

00:03:16.237 --> 00:03:17.405
not effective at all. Right.

00:03:17.405 --> 00:03:18.281
Which is what happened

00:03:18.281 --> 00:03:20.825
with the election law. That's right.

00:03:20.825 --> 00:03:21.284
Yeah.

00:03:21.659 --> 00:03:22.285
So what do you think?

00:03:22.285 --> 00:03:23.411
You think voters are listening

00:03:23.411 --> 00:03:24.287
to him, to Christie

00:03:24.287 --> 00:03:26.080
because the polls show

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:27.665
that most of these Republicans

00:03:27.665 --> 00:03:29.167
don't believe Trump did anything wrong.

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:30.001
They they do.

00:03:30.001 --> 00:03:30.877
They do believe that.

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:31.628
And I think

00:03:31.628 --> 00:03:31.961
I think

00:03:31.961 --> 00:03:32.962
ultimately he's

00:03:32.962 --> 00:03:34.255
talking to suburban

00:03:34.255 --> 00:03:35.465
voters, maybe independent

00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:36.549
voters, Republicans

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:37.550
that are persuadable,

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.676
I guess, or independent

00:03:38.676 --> 00:03:39.844
people that are persuadable.

00:03:39.844 --> 00:03:40.637
And that's what I think

00:03:40.637 --> 00:03:41.471
he's talking about, is

00:03:41.471 --> 00:03:43.139
that people are tired of it.

00:03:43.139 --> 00:03:44.599
And I have several Trump

00:03:44.599 --> 00:03:45.642
fans in my family.

00:03:45.642 --> 00:03:46.726
And I think they're tired of it.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.269
They're tired of the cases.

00:03:48.269 --> 00:03:49.145
They they certainly aren't

00:03:49.145 --> 00:03:51.147
rallying around Trump the way they were.

00:03:51.147 --> 00:03:52.690
What do you think of Trump today?

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:53.024
You know,

00:03:53.024 --> 00:03:54.025
going out there

00:03:54.025 --> 00:03:56.236
and suggesting he's some sort of martyr,

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.195
I think,

00:03:57.612 --> 00:03:59.906
and then getting into a giant limo tour

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.032
and his own plane

00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:02.951
with tons of lawyers?

00:04:02.951 --> 00:04:04.035
I don't know I think

00:04:04.035 --> 00:04:04.827
I think the thing is

00:04:04.827 --> 00:04:05.912
people are tired of it.

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.080
There's sort of this silent

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:07.872
majority of people

00:04:07.872 --> 00:04:08.665
who are tired of anything.

00:04:08.665 --> 00:04:09.666
They worry about their kids.

00:04:09.666 --> 00:04:11.751
They worry about the economy, their jobs.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:14.504
I think they're tired of the circus.

00:04:14.504 --> 00:04:15.838
And that's what it is, is a circus.

